  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Up The Wolves** (1 review): Between songs, the singer joked about forgetting the first line, then listed teenage excesses like speed, vodka and long sleepless stretches; front row was asked for the opening line [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Transjordanian Blues**: back after 90 archived shows (2261 days); rare: 12 archived performances [3]\n- **Dinu Lipatti's Bones**: back after 33 archived shows (928 days) [3]\n- **Balance**: back after 79 archived shows (1806 days); rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Wizard Buys a Hat**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Cotton**: back after 32 archived shows (924 days) [3]\n- **Young Caesar 2000**: back after 71 archived shows (1556 days); rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **The Last Day of Jimi Hendrix's Life**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Alibi**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **MountainGoats2008-05-16.nyctaper** (recommended): audience recording; 16 songs; 70 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The uploader notes the recording includes the stage moment where the singer forgets a song's first line [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **MountainGoats2008-05-16.nyctaper**: taped by nyctaper; transferred by nyctaper; source: AUD [1]. Also: Recorded about ten feet from the right PA stacks with DPA 4021 mics into an Edirol UA-5 with Oade Digimod, at 24-bit 48kHz; Transfer chain went through Soundforge for level boost, fades and resampling, then CDWave tracking, and was encoded to FLAC at level 7 [1]",
